// Procedural grass materials for ProceduralFoliageVolumeComponent.
// All use the Wind HLMS (HLMS_USER0) so blades sway via WindComponent.
//
// Property notes:
//   cull_mode none          : blades visible from both sides (single-sided quads)
//   alpha_hash yes          : dithered alpha cutout -- removes the popping/
//                             aliasing edge of hard alpha_test, especially
//                             noticeable on thin grass blade silhouettes.
//                             alpha_hash is an OPAQUE technique: it writes
//                             depth normally and needs NO blend mode and NO
//                             back-to-front sorting.
//   // alpha_to_coverage msaa_only : combines with MSAA for smoother edges
//
//   IMPORTANT: do NOT combine alpha_hash with scene_blend alpha_blend.
//   alpha_hash already converts the texture alpha into a per-pixel
//   stochastic pass/discard decision and writes depth like normal opaque
//   geometry. Adding real alpha blending on top makes each blade's
//   surviving fragments blend inconsistently against whatever happened to
//   be drawn before it (since transparent draws are not depth-sorted),
//   which is exactly what caused grass to look "see-through" to the
//   terrain in patches. Leaving scene_blend at its opaque default
//   (one zero) fixes this completely -- alpha_hash on its own already
//   gives correct, fully opaque-looking cutout grass with smooth edges.
//
//   specular_map reuses diffuse: cheap approximation, fine for distant grass
//   No normal_map: skipped per request, saves a texture fetch per pixel,
//                  grass blades are too small/thin for normal mapping to matter

hlms SwayingGrass1Material Wind
{
	cull_mode	none
	alpha_hash yes
	// alpha_to_coverage msaa_only

	diffuse_map	grass1.png
	specular_map grass1.png
}

